---
/**
 * The one closing CTA, merged from what used to be two adjacent sections
 * ("Know a tool we're missing?" and the email-alerts panel).
 *
 * Both of those resolved to the same working destination — /contact — and one
 * of them was the largest cobalt-tinted panel on the page despite every
 * control inside it being disabled. They are now two cells of one lattice, on
 * paper rather than a cobalt wash.
 *
 * The email field stays disabled and stays labelled as disabled. There is no
 * mailing list, so the field does nothing, the button says so, and the note
 * under it explains why in plain words. The dashed border is the visual
 * signal that it is not a live control.
 */
---

<section class="contrib">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="contrib-head" data-rise>
      <h2>Nothing here is final</h2>
      <p>
        Picks come out when they stop earning the slot, and a category goes in when there is
        a real shortlist to show. Tell us what to look at, or ask to hear when something
        moves.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="contrib-lattice" data-rise>
      <div class="contrib-cell">
        <h3>Tell us what we’re missing</h3>
        <p class="contrib-lede">
          Say what you use and what it replaced. We read every one, and the ones that change
          a shortlist get added with the reasoning shown.
        </p>
        <p class="contrib-act">
          <a href="/contact" class="pill pill-line">Suggest a tool</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="contrib-cell">
        <h3>Hear when a pick changes</h3>
        <p class="contrib-lede">
          We add a category or swap a pick every few weeks. One short note when that happens
          — what changed, and why it changed.
        </p>

        <div class="contrib-form">
          <label class="contrib-field">
            <span class="sr">Email address</span>
            <input
              type="email"
              placeholder="you@yourcompany.com"
              disabled
              aria-describedby="contrib-note"
            />
          </label>
          <button type="button" class="pill contrib-btn" disabled>Not open yet</button>
        </div>

        <p class="contrib-note" id="contrib-note">
          There is no mailing list running yet, so this field does nothing on purpose — we
          would rather show you the plan than collect an address we cannot mail. <a
            href="/contact"
            class="tlink">Ask us directly</a
          > and we will add you by hand.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .contrib {
    padding-block: 0 clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }

  .contrib-head h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.2vw, 2.35rem);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .contrib-head p {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    max-width: 58ch;
    color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-brand-text) 70%, transparent);
  }

  /* The shared-hairline lattice again, at two cells. */
  .contrib-lattice {
    margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .contrib-cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    background: var(--color-brand-bg);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2.75vw, 2rem);
  }

  .contrib-cell h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contrib-lede {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-brand-text) 68%, transparent);
  }

  /* Sits directly under its own copy rather than being pushed to a shared
     bottom rail: the two cells carry quite different amounts of text, and
     bottom-aligning left a hole in the middle of the shorter one. */
  .contrib-act {
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
  }

  .contrib-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 27rem;
  }

  /* Dashed, not solid: the border is the signal that this control is not
     live. */
  .contrib-field {
    flex: 1 1 12rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 3rem;
    padding-inline: 0.95rem;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, white 70%, transparent);
    border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .contrib-field input {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    outline: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-brand-muted);
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .contrib-btn {
    flex: none;
    min-height: 3rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border-color: var(--line-strong);
    color: var(--color-brand-muted);
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }

  .contrib-note {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    max-width: 50ch;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-brand-muted);
  }

  @media (min-width: 54rem) {
    .contrib-lattice {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
